{
  "dom_id": "step-q185118",
  "name": "Question 4",
  "problem": "What is the missing number?\n\n{{field-1}}\n$%$ of $50=6$",
  "worked_solution": "We can write the given problem as the following product:\n\n$$\n\\boxed{}\\,%\\times 50=6\n$$\n\nUsing the relationship between multiplication and division, we can write our problem as:\n\n$$\n\\boxed{}\\,%=6÷50=\\frac{6}{50}\n$$\n\nTo write this fraction as a percentage, we write an equivalent fraction with $100$ as the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\frac{6}{50}=\\frac{6\\times 2}{50\\times 2}=\\frac{12}{100}\n$$\n\nNow we can write this fraction as a percentage:\n\n$$\n\\frac{12}{100}=12\\,%\n$$",
